---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

/*
 * The public twin of src/pages/Privacy.tsx in the amor-budget app repo. Same
 * facts, same wording, two places, because Apple needs a URL and the user needs
 * the screen. Change one and change the other, or the app will be telling
 * somebody something this page contradicts.
 *
 * Every claim is checkable in the app's code: no bank connection, row-level
 * security on every table, no analytics dependency, and the widget's copy of
 * the figures erased on sign-out.
 */
const email = site.contactEmail;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Amor Budget"
  description="What Amor Budget collects, where it is stored, who else can see it, and how to delete it."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  updated="August 16, 2026"
>
  <p>
    Amor Budget tracks a budget you type in yourself. This page says what we hold, where it sits, who else can see
    it, and how you get rid of it.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Your email address, so you can sign in. Sign in with Apple or Google instead and we receive whatever address
      that provider hands us. Your Apple or Google password never reaches us.
    </li>
    <li>
      Your password, if you set one, stored as a hash by our authentication provider. Nobody at Amor Budget can
      read it back.
    </li>
    <li>
      Your name, if you give one or your sign-in provider passes it along. It greets you on your own Home screen
      and goes nowhere else.
    </li>
    <li>
      The money you enter: income, expenses, categories, merchant names you type, savings accounts, bills, and the
      Needs, Wants and Savings split you choose. We never connect to a bank and never ask for a banking login.
    </li>
    <li>
      A push token for your device, if you switch on reminders. Apple needs it to deliver the notification and we
      use it for nothing else.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where it sits</h2>
  <p>
    Your account and everything in it lives with Supabase, who provide our database and sign-in. Row-level security
    guards every table and is scoped to your account, so another user cannot read your rows even if they go
    looking.
  </p>
  <p>
    The home screen widget works differently. Your phone keeps today's Wants figures in a private container that
    only Amor Budget and its widget can open. That copy stays on the device, travels to no server, and is wiped
    when you sign out.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
  <p>
    We sell your data to nobody and hand it to no advertiser. The app carries no analytics and no advertising code,
    so nothing here follows you between apps or across the web.
  </p>
  <p>
    Three outside parties touch it at all: Supabase, who store it; Apple, who deliver your reminders if you turn
    them on; and Apple or Google, if you use one of them to sign in.
  </p>

  <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>
    Open Profile in the app and delete your account. That erases every transaction, budget, recurring bill and
    savings account you have entered, and we cannot bring any of it back. Prefer that we do it for you? Write to{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> and we will.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Amor Budget is built for adults managing their own money. We do not aim it at children under 13 and we do not
    knowingly keep their data. Tell us at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> if a child has made an account
    and we will remove it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    When what we collect changes, this page changes with it and the date at the top moves. The same text appears
    inside the app, under Profile.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Anything here unclear, or want to know what we hold on you? Reach us at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
